Sensitive Personal Information. We do not use or disclose sensitive personal information for purposes other than those
specified in the CCPA.
Categories Of Sources. We collect this personal information from the following categories of sources:
Consumers;
Advertising networks;
Analytics providers;
Businesses and education institutions associated with consumers;
Business partners;
Service providers; and
Affiliates not under the Instructure brand.
Why We Collect, Use, Sell, and Share California Information.
We use and disclose all categories of personal information we collect for our commercial and business purposes, as
further described in the Instructure Marketing Privacy Policy. These commercial and business purposes for which we
use and disclose these categories of personal information include, without limitation:
Our commercial purposes, which include:
Personalized marketing and advertising, including sending surveys and promotional communications and soliciting
feedback;
Enabling commercial transactions and sending administrative email;
Responding to requests made by consumers including to respond to comments and inquiries; and
Operating, maintaining, and improving our websites and services including personalization.
Our business purposes as identified in the CCPA, which include:
Auditing related to our interactions with you;
Ensuring the security and integrity of our systems;
Legal compliance;
Detecting and protecting against security incidents, fraud, and illegal activity;
Debugging;

Performing services (for us or our service provider) such as account servicing, processing orders and payments, and
analytics;
Internal research for technological improvement;
Internal operations;
Activities to maintain and improve our services; and
Other one-time uses.
We sold or shared personal information to third parties for the following business or commercial purposes:
Analytics related to the use of the Site and marketing; and
Advancing our commercial or economic interests, including by marketing our product and services.
We do not sell the personal information of minors we know to be under 16 years of age.
Recipients Of California Personal Information.
We disclose the categories of personal information designated above to the categories of third parties listed below for
business purposes:
Service providers;
Affiliates not under the Instructure brand;
Third parties at your request or direction;
Data analytics providers;
Partners; and
Social networks.
We sell or share the categories of personal information designated above to the categories of third parties listed below:
Advertising/marketing companies;
Advertising networks;
Business services/agencies;
Business to business companies;
Marketing data companies;
Data analytics providers;
Social networks; and
Educational institutions & companies.
Your Rights Regarding Personal Information.
California residents have certain rights with respect to the personal information collected by businesses. If you are a
California resident, you may exercise the following rights regarding your personal information, subject to certain
exceptions and limitations:
The right to know the categories and specific pieces of personal information we collect, use, disclose, and sell about you,
the categories of sources from which we collected your personal information, our purposes for collecting or selling your
personal information, the categories of your personal information that we have either sold or disclosed for a business
purpose, and the categories of third parties with which we have shared personal information;
The right to correct inaccurate personal information that we maintain about you;
The right to request that we delete the personal information we have collected from you;
The right to opt out of our sale or sharing of your personal information. Please note that if you opt out of certain types of
